From 349045ec8b713e9d935d836e74610f84b09f0c91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gtguerreiro-max <295622337+gtguerreiro-max@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:02:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/51] gpu: texture fetches and shader ops as Xenia canary has
 them

Ported from Xenia canary's DXBC translator (BSD), for both the Xenos plugin and a host renderer
that uses the translator:

- Texture fetches return what Xenos returns, from a per fetch constant
  SystemConstants::texture_integer_scale_bits (rex/xenos/texture_integer_scale.h, canary's
  GetIntegerScaleBits; d119505, 0c843ef, c3cd861, e6cd2e4): fraction fetches round unsigned
  components to 16 fractional bits (Forza Horizon's motion blur compares a point-sampled 0x80
  with 32897 / 65536, its Q16 value; the host's 128 / 255 is just below it), integer fetches
  scale each component by its own width through the swizzle and round point-sampled ones,
  unsigned-biased components decode as signed offset binary (an 8-bit 128 reads 0), and
  point-sampled 4 to 6 bit unsigned components read as n * (2^w + 1) / 2^(2w). The D3D12
  backend fills the constant and no longer folds integer scales into exp_adjust
  (integer_fetch.h stays for Vulkan). Replaces 0046's (x + (x >> 7)) / 256 and its
  Modification::pixel.textures_unorm8.
- A two-component scalar op's second operand is Z when the paired vector op uses source 3
  (92ada8e), in the translator and the interpreter.
- Signed memexport: the copysign rounding bias goes into its temp, not over the value (da47dfa).
- Vertex words at or past the fetch constant's size read 0 (9e9d3cd).
- A stacked texture's layer is clamped to its layers' centres (04085ef: 584107FB's backdrop).
- An unnormalized 2D fetch locked to one mip divides by that mip's size (8486e97).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
